<body>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">title: "Bathroom Remodel Cost Breakdown: Real Prices for Tile, Vanities, Fixtures &amp; Labor" description: "Complete bathroom renovation cost breakdown with actual material prices, labor rates, and contractor red flags. Budget from $6K to $40K+ based on scope." date: 2024-01-20 author: Ungouge Team keywords: ["bathroom remodel cost breakdown", "bathroom renovation cost", "how much does bathroom remodel cost", "bathroom remodel budget", "bathroom renovation prices"]</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h1 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.1px 0.0px; font: 24.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #138756; -webkit-text-stroke: #138756"><span class="s1"><b>Bathroom Remodel Cost Breakdown: Real Prices for Tile, Vanities, Fixtures &amp; Labor</b></span></h1>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You've gotten quotes for a bathroom remodel that range from $8,000 to $35,000. Same space. Similar materials. How can the difference be that extreme?</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Bathroom remodels are a goldmine for contractor padding. There are dozens of specialized tasks—plumbing, tile work, electrical, waterproofing—and most homeowners have no idea what each should cost.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">This guide breaks down every component of a bathroom remodel with real market data: material costs, labor rates, and exactly where contractors inflate quotes. You'll know what's fair and what's gouging.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Bathroom Remodel Cost Overview by Scope</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Before itemizing costs, here are realistic budgets by project scope:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td1">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Scope</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td2">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Budget Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td3">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-Range Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td4">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>High-End Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Powder Room (20-30 sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$3,000-$6,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$6,000-$12,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$12,000-$25,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Small Full Bath (35-50 sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$6,000-$12,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$12,000-$22,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$22,000-$40,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Master Bath (75-120 sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$12,000-$22,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$22,000-$45,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$45,000-$100,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What defines each tier:</b></span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget:</b> Prefab shower/tub, stock vanity, vinyl flooring, basic tile, minimal layout changes</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-Range:</b> Tile shower with glass door, semi-custom vanity, ceramic/porcelain tile flooring, upgraded fixtures, some layout adjustments</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>High-End:</b> Custom tile shower with frameless glass, custom vanity, marble/stone flooring, luxury fixtures, significant layout changes</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>The Itemized Breakdown: Where Your Money Goes</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Tile Work (15-25% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Tile is the most visible element in a bathroom and often where costs escalate dramatically.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Floor Tile</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Ceramic/Porcelain (Budget-Mid)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $2-$8 per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $5-$12 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $7-$20 per sq ft - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $350-$1,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Natural Stone (Mid-High)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $5-$25 per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $8-$18 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $13-$43 per sq ft - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $650-$2,150</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Luxury Tile (High-End)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $15-$50+ per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $12-$25 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $27-$75+ per sq ft - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $1,350-$3,750+</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Shower/Tub Surround Tile</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Standard Ceramic (Budget)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $3-$10 per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $10-$15 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $13-$25 per sq ft - <b>80 sq ft shower:</b> $1,040-$2,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Designer Subway/Mosaic (Mid-Range)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $8-$20 per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $12-$20 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $20-$40 per sq ft - <b>80 sq ft shower:</b> $1,600-$3,200</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Natural Stone/Marble (High-End)</b> - <b>Material:</b> $15-$60 per square foot - <b>Installation:</b> $15-$30 per square foot - <b>Total installed:</b> $30-$90 per sq ft - <b>80 sq ft shower:</b> $2,400-$7,200</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What's included in installation:</b> - Surface preparation - Waterproofing/cement board - Thin-set mortar - Tile cutting and layout - Grout and sealing</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flags:</b> - Charging $25+ per sq ft to install basic ceramic tile (standard is $10-$15) - Separate charges for waterproofing when it's included in "installed" price - "Prep work" fees exceeding $500 for standard bathroom</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Vanity &amp; Countertop (10-20% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Vanities range from $200 stock units to $5,000+ custom pieces.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Stock Vanity (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $200-$800 (vanity only) - 24-48" width - Particle board or MDF - Basic hardware - Cultured marble top often included</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> Home Depot Hampton Bay, Glacier Bay, IKEA</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Semi-Custom Vanity (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $800-$2,500 (vanity only) - 30-60" width - Plywood construction - Soft-close drawers - More finish options</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> KraftMaid, Bertch, Thomasville</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Custom Vanity (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $2,000-$6,000+ (vanity only) - Any size - Solid wood construction - Hand-crafted details - Unique finishes</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Countertop Materials</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cultured Marble (Budget)</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $40-$80 per sq ft installed - <b>8 sq ft vanity top:</b> $320-$640 - Integrated sink, seamless - Can scratch/stain</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Quartz (Mid-Range)</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $60-$120 per sq ft installed - <b>8 sq ft vanity top:</b> $480-$960 - Non-porous, low maintenance - Modern, consistent appearance</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Natural Stone (High-End)</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $75-$200 per sq ft installed - <b>8 sq ft vanity top:</b> $600-$1,600 - Unique, luxurious - Requires sealing</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Installation Labor</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $200-$500 - Remove old vanity - Install new vanity and countertop - Connect plumbing - Level and secure - 2-4 hours</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $800 for vanity installation with no plumbing relocation.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Shower/Tub (15-30% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">The shower or tub is often the centerpiece—and the most complex component.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Prefab Shower/Tub Combo (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $600-$1,500 (unit + installation) - <b>Unit:</b> $300-$800 - <b>Installation:</b> $300-$700 - Acrylic or fiberglass - Easy to install - Limited design options</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Alcove Tub Replacement (Budget-Mid)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $800-$2,500 (tub + installation) - <b>Tub:</b> $300-$1,200 - <b>Installation:</b> $500-$1,300 - Cast iron, acrylic, or fiberglass - Standard sizes (60" x 30") - Surround must be separate</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Tile Shower with Fiberglass Base (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $3,000-$6,000 (complete) - <b>Shower pan:</b> $300-$600 - <b>Tile work:</b> $1,600-$3,200 - <b>Glass door:</b> $700-$1,500 - <b>Fixtures:</b> $400-$700 - Custom appearance without full custom cost</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Custom Tile Shower (Mid-High)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $5,000-$12,000 (complete) - <b>Tile pan (custom):</b> $800-$1,800 - <b>Tile work:</b> $2,400-$6,000 - <b>Frameless glass door:</b> $1,200-$2,500 - <b>Fixtures:</b> $600-$1,700 - Any size, full customization</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Luxury Walk-In Shower (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $10,000-$25,000+ (complete) - <b>Custom pan/curbless:</b> $1,500-$3,500 - <b>Premium tile work:</b> $4,000-$10,000 - <b>Frameless glass:</b> $2,000-$4,000 - <b>Luxury fixtures (body sprays, rain head):</b> $2,500-$7,500 - Spa-like features</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Freestanding Tub (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $2,500-$8,000 (tub + installation) - <b>Tub:</b> $1,500-$5,000 - <b>Plumbing (floor-mount filler):</b> $500-$1,500 - <b>Installation:</b> $500-$1,500 - Acrylic, stone, or cast iron - Statement piece</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flags:</b> - Charging $2,000 to install a prefab shower (should be $300-$700) - "Waterproofing" listed separately when included in tile installation - Glass door quotes 2x higher than retail (Lowe's/Home Depot prices are transparent)</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Plumbing (15-25% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Plumbing is where costs explode if you're relocating fixtures.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Fixture Replacement (No Relocation)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Toilet Installation</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $150-$400 (labor only) - Remove old toilet - Install new wax ring - Set new toilet - Connect water supply - 1-2 hours</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Sink/Faucet Installation</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $200-$500 (labor only) - Remove old sink/faucet - Install new fixtures - Connect supply and drain - 2-3 hours</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Shower Valve Replacement</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $300-$800 (labor only) - Access behind wall (cutting/patching) - Replace valve body - Connect to existing plumbing - Test for leaks - 3-5 hours</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Fixture Relocation (Major Cost)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Relocating Toilet</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $1,500-$4,000 - Rerouting drain (3" pipe) - Relocating water supply - May require breaking concrete slab - Permits and inspections</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Relocating Shower/Tub</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $2,000-$6,000 - Drain and supply relocation - Waterproofing new area - Wall framing adjustments - Extensive labor</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>New Bathroom Addition</b> - <b>Cost:</b> $3,000-$10,000 (plumbing rough-in) - Running new supply lines - Installing new drain/vent stacks - Connecting to main sewer - Code compliance and permits</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical plumber hourly rate:</b> $75-$150 per hour (varies by region)</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $1,200 to replace a toilet when no relocation is involved. Standard is $150-$400.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Electrical (5-10% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Bathrooms require GFCI outlets, proper lighting, and ventilation.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Outlet Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $100-$250 per outlet - GFCI required within 6 feet of water - Includes box, outlet, wiring - 1-2 hours per outlet</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Vanity Lighting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$400 per fixture (labor only) - Mounting electrical box - Wiring to switch - Installing fixture - 1-2 hours per fixture</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Recessed Lighting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$350 per light - Moisture-rated housing required - Cutting ceiling hole - Wiring to switch - 2-3 hours per light</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Exhaust Fan Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $200-$600 (fan + installation) - <b>Fan:</b> $50-$250 - <b>Installation:</b> $150-$350 - Ductwork to exterior vent - Electrical connection - Code-required in most areas</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Heated Floor Installation (Electrical)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $10-$20 per sq ft (materials + labor) - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $500-$1,000 - Electric heating mat under tile - Dedicated circuit and thermostat - Installed during tile work</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical electrician hourly rate:</b> $75-$150 per hour</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $500 to install a single outlet. Unless significant rewiring is needed, this is padding.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Flooring (5-10% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Bathroom flooring must handle moisture and temperature changes.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Vinyl/LVP (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $3-$8 per sq ft installed - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $150-$400 - Waterproof, durable - Easy installation</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Ceramic/Porcelain Tile (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $7-$20 per sq ft installed - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $350-$1,000 - Highly durable, waterproof - Classic appearance</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Natural Stone (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $13-$40 per sq ft installed - <b>50 sq ft bathroom:</b> $650-$2,000 - Luxurious, unique - Requires sealing</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Installation labor typically:</b> $5-$12 per sq ft depending on material</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $15+ per sq ft to install vinyl flooring. Standard LVP installation is $3-$5 per sq ft.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>7. Fixtures &amp; Hardware (5-10% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">The small stuff adds up quickly.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Toilets</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Budget (2-piece):</b> $100-$300</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range (1-piece):</b> $300-$800</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>High-end (wall-mount, bidet):</b> $800-$3,000+</span></li>
</ul>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Faucets</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Budget:</b> $50-$150</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range:</b> $150-$400</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>High-end:</b> $400-$1,500+</span></li>
</ul>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Showerheads</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Budget:</b> $20-$75</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range (rain head):</b> $75-$300</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>High-end (body sprays, digital):</b> $300-$2,500+</span></li>
</ul>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Towel Bars, Toilet Paper Holder, Robe Hooks</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Budget set:</b> $30-$100</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range set:</b> $100-$300</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>High-end set:</b> $300-$1,000+</span></li>
</ul>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Mirrors &amp; Medicine Cabinets</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Budget:</b> $50-$200</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range:</b> $200-$600</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"><b></b></span><span class="s1"><b>High-end (custom, LED-lit):</b> $600-$2,500+</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Contractor charging $200 to install a towel bar. Standard installation is $30-$75.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>8. Labor (20-30% of budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Beyond specialized trades, general contractor labor includes:</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Demolition</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $500-$1,500 - Remove old fixtures, tile, flooring - Haul away debris - Dumpster rental: $200-$400 - 1-2 days</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Drywall Repair &amp; Painting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $800-$2,000 - Patching walls after demo - Skim coating - Moisture-resistant paint (2 coats) - 2-3 days</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>General Carpentry</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $50-$100 per hour - Framing adjustments - Installing trim/molding - Hanging doors - Miscellaneous adjustments</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> "Labor" line items without task-specific breakdown. Insist on details.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Small vs. Medium vs. Large Bathroom Budgets</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Powder Room Remodel (20-30 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget ($3,000-$6,000):</b> - Toilet replacement: $300-$600 - Stock vanity (24"): $400-$800 - Vinyl flooring: $150-$300 - Basic mirror/lighting: $150-$400 - Paint: $200-$400 - Labor (demo, install, paint): $1,200-$2,500 - Permits/contingency: $600-$1,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($6,000-$12,000):</b> - Upgraded toilet: $500-$1,000 - Semi-custom vanity: $800-$1,800 - Tile flooring: $300-$700 - Designer mirror/lighting: $400-$1,000 - Custom paint/wallpaper: $400-$800 - Labor: $2,500-$5,000 - Permits/contingency: $1,100-$2,700</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Small Full Bath Remodel (35-50 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget ($6,000-$12,000):</b> - Prefab tub/shower: $900-$1,800 - Toilet: $300-$600 - Stock vanity: $400-$900 - Vinyl flooring: $200-$450 - Basic tile surround: $800-$1,500 - Fixtures/hardware: $300-$700 - Labor: $2,500-$4,500 - Permits/contingency: $600-$2,500</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($12,000-$22,000):</b> - Tile shower with glass door: $3,500-$6,500 - Upgraded toilet: $400-$900 - Semi-custom vanity: $1,000-$2,200 - Tile flooring: $500-$1,200 - Designer fixtures: $600-$1,400 - Labor: $4,500-$7,500 - Permits/contingency: $1,500-$4,300</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Master Bath Remodel (75-120 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget ($12,000-$22,000):</b> - Prefab shower + tub: $1,800-$3,500 - Dual vanity (stock): $1,000-$2,200 - Toilet: $300-$700 - Vinyl flooring: $400-$800 - Basic tile work: $1,500-$3,000 - Fixtures/hardware: $600-$1,300 - Labor: $5,000-$8,500 - Permits/contingency: $1,400-$3,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($22,000-$45,000):</b> - Custom tile shower: $6,000-$11,000 - Soaking tub: $1,500-$3,500 - Dual vanity (semi-custom): $2,000-$4,500 - Tile flooring: $1,200-$2,500 - Designer fixtures: $1,500-$3,500 - Labor: $8,000-$15,000 - Permits/contingency: $2,800-$7,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>High-end ($45,000-$100,000+):</b> - Luxury walk-in shower: $12,000-$22,000 - Freestanding tub: $3,500-$8,000 - Custom dual vanity: $4,000-$10,000 - Marble/stone flooring: $2,000-$5,000 - Heated floors: $1,000-$2,500 - Premium fixtures: $3,000-$8,000 - Extensive layout changes: $5,000-$12,000 - Labor: $15,000-$30,000 - Permits/contingency: $9,500-$25,000</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Where Contractors Pad Bathroom Quotes</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Based on thousands of quote analyses, here's where padding is most common:</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Tile Installation Labor</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Quoting $25-$35 per sq ft for basic ceramic tile installation.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Standard ceramic tile installation is $10-$15 per sq ft, including prep and waterproofing.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Ask for per-square-foot breakdown and compare to industry standards.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Separate "Waterproofing" Charges</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Adding $800-$1,500 for waterproofing when it's already included in tile installation.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Waterproofing (cement board, RedGard, etc.) is part of standard tile prep.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> If waterproofing is listed separately, verify what's included in tile labor.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Glass Door Markups</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Charging $2,500 for a frameless glass door that retails for $1,200.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Reasonable markup is 20-40%. You can verify door prices online (Home Depot, Lowe's, specialty shops).</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Research the specific door model and compare prices.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Plumbing "Surprises"</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Discovering "hidden issues" after demo that require $2,000-$5,000 in additional plumbing work.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Some issues are legitimate, but experienced contractors should identify most problems upfront.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Include a clause in your contract requiring written approval before additional work exceeding $500.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Vague "Prep Work" Fees</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> $1,200 "prep work" charge with no itemization.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Prep is included in tile installation, or should be itemized (demo, cement board, etc.).</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Demand task-specific breakdown for any "prep" or "miscellaneous" charges.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Permit Padding</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Charging $800 for permits that cost $200.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Reality:</b> Bathroom permits typically cost $100-$400 depending on municipality.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Call your local building department and verify permit costs.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Money-Saving Tips Without Sacrificing Quality</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Keep the Layout</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Moving plumbing is the single biggest cost driver. If you can work with your existing layout, you'll save $3,000-$8,000.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Choose Prefab Where It Doesn't Show</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">A prefab shower base under beautiful tile looks identical to a custom pan—and saves $500-$1,200.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Buy Fixtures Yourself</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Contractors mark up toilets, faucets, and lighting 30-50%. Buy during sales and save $500-$2,000.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Do Your Own Demo</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Bathroom demo is labor-intensive but not technically difficult. Doing it yourself saves $500-$1,200.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What you'll need:</b> - Basic tools (pry bar, hammer, utility knife, screwdriver) - Safety gear (gloves, goggles, respirator) - Dumpster rental ($200-$400) - 1-2 days of hard work</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Tile Only Where It Matters</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Full-wall tile in the shower is beautiful, but tiling to 6 feet instead of ceiling height saves $400-$1,000 in materials and labor.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Choose Porcelain Over Natural Stone</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Modern porcelain tile mimics marble and stone beautifully—at 40-60% less cost and with no sealing required.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>7. Refinish Instead of Replace</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">If your tub is structurally sound, professional refinishing costs $400-$600 vs. $800-$2,500 for replacement.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>8. Skip Heated Floors</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">They're luxurious but add $500-$1,500. A heated towel rack delivers warmth for $200-$400.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>9. Use Semi-Custom Vanities</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Semi-custom vanities look nearly identical to custom and cost 40-60% less.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>10. Get Three Quotes</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">This is non-negotiable. Three quotes from licensed, insured contractors will show you the fair market range.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline Expectations</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Understanding realistic timelines helps you spot padding or overbooked contractors.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Powder Room</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 1-2 weeks - Days 1-2: Demo - Days 3-5: Plumbing, electrical, drywall - Days 6-8: Tile work - Days 9-10: Fixtures, paint, final touches</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Small Full Bath</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 2-3 weeks - Week 1: Demo, rough plumbing/electrical - Week 2: Tile work (floor and shower) - Week 3: Fixtures, vanity, paint, completion</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Master Bath</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 3-5 weeks - Week 1: Demo and rough work - Week 2-3: Tile work (extensive) - Week 4: Fixtures, vanity, custom elements - Week 5: Final touches, punch list</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> If a contractor says a powder room will take 8 weeks, they're overbooked or padding the timeline.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Verify Your Bathroom Remodel Quote</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Analyzing a multi-page quote with dozens of specialized line items is overwhelming. That's why we built <b>Ungouge.ai</b>.</span></p>
